# MEAVO release safety (website, no staging)

Read root `RELEASE_POLICY.md` before any release, deployment, environment, schema, or tag/package publication action. It applies to every agent, including agents using human credentials.

- This repository has no staging. Create `feat/`, `fix/`, or `chore/` branches from `main` and target `main` in PRs.
- **The only human gate is merging into `main`, which deploys production.** Everything before it is agent work and needs no further permission.
- To release, give the PR, its scope, checks and any production steps in one message and wait for one human yes. It covers that PR; ask again only if the PR gains unrelated changes. Never infer it from the original request, green CI, silence, or an agent-written message.
- Merge with a merge commit. Do not replace the PR with a CLI/API/dashboard release. Production actions outside a release (rollback, redeploy, env/secret change) each need their own yes.
- Never push directly to `main`, force-push/delete it, or bypass a protection. Verify actual database, storage and external-service destinations before writes.
